1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,883
At two-thirteen in the morning, the

2
00:00:02,883 --> 00:00:04,935
bell rings at pump four.

3
00:00:06,565 --> 00:00:08,224
That bell means somebody

4
00:00:08,224 --> 00:00:10,033
just lifted a nozzle.

5
00:00:10,163 --> 00:00:12,508
I look up from the register.

6
00:00:12,638 --> 00:00:15,101
There's no car at pump four.

7
00:00:15,231 --> 00:00:16,553
There's a man.

8
00:00:17,083 --> 00:00:19,258
He's holding the nozzle against his

9
00:00:19,258 --> 00:00:21,220
chest, like he's hugging it,

10
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:23,708
and he's staring at the store.

11
00:00:23,838 --> 00:00:26,554
Not at me. At the glass.

12
00:00:27,184 --> 00:00:28,625
I don't move.

13
00:00:28,755 --> 00:00:30,713
My headlamp is off. The

14
00:00:30,713 --> 00:00:32,430
store lights are off.

15
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,696
Out there, under the canopy,

16
00:00:34,696 --> 00:00:36,555
it's bright as noon.

17
00:00:37,085 --> 00:00:38,870
He leans closer.

18
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,259
His nose touches the window.

19
00:00:41,989 --> 00:00:43,444
And all he sees...

20
00:00:44,274 --> 00:00:45,760
is himself.

21
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:48,876
There are always others.
